Subject: [PATCH 51/53] B70-SM: top-k-first temperature sampling and
 spec-decode verification (B70_SAMPLER_FAST=1, default off)

Three launches replace the fp32 copy, temperature kernel, Qrita top-k/top-p, stats,
rejection, resample and insert kernels: split top-k (tile-wise, ties to the lower id),
merge + softmax + top-p on the k-token support, and the Leviathan test + residual
resample evaluated on that support with the DFlash2 cached candidates as the draft
support. Same murmur3 u / Gumbel streams as stock. Plain sampler gets the same support.
Falls back to stock for min_p, processed logprobs, top-k-disabled sampled rows, k>32,
grammar, block/synthetic/adaptive verification, watermarking, fp64 Gumbel.
Warmup compiles KP 16 and 32 in xpu_filter_warmup. Unset = unchanged behaviour.
